The numbers is a list of 1, 3, and 6.
The slack is 3.
Sort numbers.
The last is the last position of numbers.
The best is item last of numbers minus item 0 of numbers.
For every spot from 0 to last minus 1.
The low is item 0 of numbers plus slack.
The high is item last of numbers minus slack.
If item (spot plus 1) of numbers minus slack is less than low, set low to item (spot plus 1) of numbers minus slack.
If item spot of numbers plus slack is more than high, set high to item spot of numbers plus slack.
The spread is high minus low.
If spread is less than best, set best to spread.

Show best.
